# Bonsol Input Resolver Standards

## Context
- Applied when implementing input resolution for RISC0 programs
- Focuses on secure handling of public and private inputs
- Ensures proper parallel processing and resource limits
- Critical for program execution security
- Integrates with Solana RPC and HTTP clients

## Requirements

### Input Type Handling
- Use proper input enum variants:
  ```rust
  pub enum ProgramInput {
      Empty,
      Resolved(ResolvedInput),
      Unresolved(UnresolvedInput),
  }
  ```
- Implement support checking:
  ```rust
  fn supports(&self, input_type: InputType) -> bool {
      match input_type {
          InputType::PublicUrl => true,
          InputType::PublicData => true,
          InputType::PublicAccountData => true,
          InputType::Private => true,
          InputType::PublicProof => true,
          _ => false,
      }
  }
  ```

### Input Resolution
- Implement parallel processing for public inputs:
  ```rust
  async fn resolve_public_inputs(
      &self,
      inputs: Vec<InputT>
  ) -> Result<Vec<ProgramInput>> {
      let mut url_set = JoinSet::new();
      let mut res = vec![ProgramInput::Empty; inputs.len()];
      
      // Process in parallel
      for (index, input) in inputs.into_iter().enumerate() {
          let client = self.http_client.clone();
          res[index] = self.par_resolve_input(
              client,
              index as u8,
              input,
              &mut url_set
          )?;
      }
      
      // Wait for completion
      while let Some(result) = url_set.join_next().await {
          match result {
              Ok(Ok(ri)) => {
                  res[ri.index as usize] = ProgramInput::Resolved(ri);
              }
              Err(e) => return Err(e.into()),
          }
      }
      Ok(res)
  }
  ```

### Private Input Security
- Implement signed requests for private inputs:
  ```rust
  let pir = PrivateInputRequest {
      identity: signer.pubkey(),
      claim_id: execution_id.to_string(),
      input_index: index,
      now_utc: SystemTime::now()
          .duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH)?
          .as_secs(),
  };
  let signature = signer.sign_message(&pir.to_bytes());
  ```

### Resource Management
- Enforce size and timeout limits:
  ```rust
  pub struct DefaultInputResolver {
      http_client: Arc<reqwest::Client>,
      solana_rpc_client: Arc<RpcClient>,
      max_input_size_mb: u32,
      timeout: Duration,
  }
  ```
- Track download progress and enforce limits
- Handle timeouts gracefully
- Clean up resources on error

## Examples

<example>
// Good: Complete input resolver implementation
pub struct CustomInputResolver {
    http_client: Arc<reqwest::Client>,
    max_size: usize,
    timeout: Duration,
}

#[async_trait]
impl InputResolver for CustomInputResolver {
    async fn resolve_public_inputs(
        &self,
        inputs: Vec<InputT>
    ) -> Result<Vec<ProgramInput>> {
        let mut url_set = JoinSet::new();
        let mut results = vec![ProgramInput::Empty; inputs.len()];
        
        // Process inputs in parallel
        for (idx, input) in inputs.into_iter().enumerate() {
            let client = self.http_client.clone();
            let max_size = self.max_size;
            let timeout = self.timeout;
            
            url_set.spawn(async move {
                match input.url {
                    Some(url) => {
                        download_with_limits(
                            client,
                            idx as u8,
                            url,
                            max_size,
                            timeout
                        ).await
                    }
                    None => Ok(ResolvedInput::empty(idx as u8)),
                }
            });
        }
        
        // Collect results with proper error handling
        while let Some(result) = url_set.join_next().await {
            match result {
                Ok(Ok(input)) => {
                    results[input.index as usize] = 
                        ProgramInput::Resolved(input);
                }
                Ok(Err(e)) => {
                    url_set.abort_all();
                    return Err(e);
                }
                Err(e) => {
                    url_set.abort_all();
                    return Err(e.into());
                }
            }
        }
        
        Ok(results)
    }
}
</example>

<example>
// Good: Resource-safe download implementation
async fn download_with_limits(
    client: Arc<reqwest::Client>,
    index: u8,
    url: Url,
    max_size: usize,
    timeout: Duration,
) -> Result<ResolvedInput> {
    let response = client
        .get(url.clone())
        .timeout(timeout)
        .send()
        .await?;
        
    if !response.status().is_success() {
        return Err(anyhow::anyhow!(
            "Failed to download input {}: {}",
            index,
            response.status()
        ));
    }
    
    let content_length = response
        .content_length()
        .unwrap_or(0);
        
    if content_length > max_size as u64 {
        return Err(anyhow::anyhow!(
            "Input {} too large: {} > {}",
            index,
            content_length,
            max_size
        ));
    }
    
    let data = response
        .bytes()
        .await?
        .to_vec();
        
    Ok(ResolvedInput {
        index,
        data,
        input_type: ProgramInputType::PublicUrl,
    })
}
</example>

<example type="invalid">
// Bad: Unsafe parallel processing
async fn resolve_unsafe(inputs: Vec<InputT>) -> Result<Vec<ProgramInput>> {
    let futures: Vec<_> = inputs
        .into_iter()
        .map(|input| async {
            // No timeout
            // No size limits
            // No error handling
            let response = reqwest::get(input.url).await?;
            let data = response.bytes().await?;
            Ok(ProgramInput::Resolved(ResolvedInput {
                index: 0, // Wrong index
                data: data.to_vec(),
                input_type: ProgramInputType::PublicUrl,
            }))
        })
        .collect();
    
    futures::future::join_all(futures).await // Can exhaust resources
}
</example>

